module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.Twist.Iso
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafSymmetricAlgebra.ProjectiveSpaceTwist
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartLocality.ChartGamma

/-!
# The module half of Tag 01OE on a chart, discharged

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SheafSymmetricAlgebra/ProjectiveSpaceTwist.lean` carries the
module half of [Stacks, Tag 01OE] — that the isomorphism `ℙⁿ_X ≅ 𝐏(𝒪_X^{n+1})` matches the two
hyperplane sheaves — as the hypothesis `Stacks.SymGraded.HasFreeBundleTwistOne`, and reduces it
over an affine base to the chartwise form `Stacks.SymGraded.HasChartTwistOne`: over each affine
open `U` of `X`, the inverse image of the integral `𝒪(1)` along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of the homogeneous coordinates
`Stacks.SymGraded.chartCoordHom n U : ℤ[T₀, …, Tₙ] →+*ᵍ Γ(U, Sym(𝒪_X^{n+1}))` is the degree-one
twist of the target graded ring.

**This file proves that chartwise statement at every scheme and every open**, and with it
`Stacks.SymGraded.HasFreeBundleTwistOne` over an affine base.

The homogeneous coordinates factor as
`chartCoordHom n U = (chartGradedHom n U).comp (coordGradedHom n U)`, and each factor is handled
by a theorem of the library:

* `Stacks.SymGraded.coordGradedHom n U` is a coefficient change and a reindexing of a polynomial
  grading, so [Stacks, Tag 01MY]'s comparison map on its twists is an isomorphism by
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartLocality.isIso_projTwistComparison` — the degree-one chart
  argument — whose one input is that the irrelevant ideal of the target is generated by images of
  degree-one elements. It is: the target's irrelevant ideal is generated by the variables, and
  each variable is the image of a variable.
* `Stacks.SymGraded.chartGradedHom n U` is an *isomorphism* of graded rings, with inverse
  `Stacks.SymGraded.chartGradedInv n U`. An isomorphism is in particular a degreewise
  localization away from `1`, so `Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.isIso_twistMap` — the proved half of
  [Stacks, Tag 01NO] — applies.

Composing the two comparisons along `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_comp` gives the chartwise
statement. Nothing here is special to the degree `1`; the degree is fixed only because
`Stacks.SymGraded.HasChartTwistOne` fixes it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SymGraded.isAwayDegreewise_chartGradedHom`: an isomorphism of graded rings is a
  degreewise localization away from `1`, for the chart comparison.
* `Stacks.SymGraded.irrelevant_le_span_image_coordGradedHom`: the irrelevant ideal of
  `Γ(X, U)[T₀, …, Tₙ]` is generated by the images of the degree-one part of `ℤ[T₀, …, Tₙ]`.
* `Stacks.SymGraded.hasChartTwistOne`: **`Stacks.SymGraded.HasChartTwistOne` is a theorem**, at
  every scheme and every `n`.
* `Stacks.SymGraded.hasFreeBundleTwistOne`: **the module half of [Stacks, Tag 01OE] over an
  affine base is a theorem.**

## Implementation notes

**No `stacks` attribute is attached.** `Stacks.SymGraded.hasFreeBundleTwistOne` is the module half
of [Stacks, Tag 01OE] over an affine base only — the general base needs the chart comparisons to
be compatible with [Stacks, Tag 01NO]'s transitions, which is the glueing step this file does not
perform — and the two assertions of Tag 01OE that are theorems at an arbitrary base already carry
the tag on `Stacks.SymGraded.projectiveBundleIsoProjectiveSpace` and
`Stacks.SymGraded.projectiveBundleIsoProjectiveSpace_hom_comp_fst`.

**`Stacks.SymGraded.irrelevant_le_span_X_of_index` is the arbitrary-index form** of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.irrelevant_le_span_X`, which is stated for the variables
`Fin (n + 1)` of projective space; the chart grading is indexed by
`Stacks.SymGraded.coordIndex n = ULift (Fin (n + 1))`, so the `Fin` form does not apply.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (twistingSheaf)

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

universe u

namespace Stacks.SymGraded

/-! ### The irrelevant ideal of a polynomial ring, at an arbitrary index type -/

/-- **The irrelevant ideal of a polynomial ring is contained in the span of the variables**, for
an arbitrary index type. This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.irrelevant_le_span_X` with the index type `Fin (n + 1)`
of projective space replaced by an arbitrary one, which is what the chart grading — indexed by
`Stacks.SymGraded.coordIndex n` — needs. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_span_X_of_index {σ : Type*} {A : Type*} [CommRing A] :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule σ A)).toIdeal ≤
      Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : σ → MvPolynomial σ A)) :=
  (HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal_irrelevant_le _).mpr fun _ hd _ hf => by
    simpa using
      Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.mem_span_X_of_mem_homogeneousSubmodule hd hf

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (n : ℕ)

/-- **The irrelevant ideal of `Γ(X, U)[T₀, …, Tₙ]` is generated by the images of the degree-one
part of `ℤ[T₀, …, Tₙ]`.** This is the hypothesis of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartLocality.isIso_projTwistComparison` for the coefficient change
and reindexing `Stacks.SymGraded.coordGradedHom`: the irrelevant ideal is generated by the
variables, and each variable is the image of the corresponding variable of `ℤ[T₀, …, Tₙ]`, which
is homogeneous of degree one. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_span_image_coordGradedHom (U : X.Opens) :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant
        (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (coordIndex.{u} n) ↥(siteRing X (op U)))).toIdeal ≤
      Ideal.span (coordGradedHom n U ''
        ((MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) (ULift.{u} ℤ) 1 : Set _))) := by
  refine irrelevant_le_span_X_of_index.trans (Ideal.span_mono ?_)
  rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨MvPolynomial.X j.down,
    (MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X _ _),
    coordGradedHom_X n U j.down⟩

/-! ### An isomorphism of graded rings is a degreewise localization away from `1` -/

/-- **The chart comparison is a degreewise localization away from `1`.** It is an isomorphism of
graded rings, with graded inverse `Stacks.SymGraded.chartGradedInv`: the image of `1` is a unit, a
homogeneous element of the target is the image of its own preimage, which is homogeneous of the
same degree, and the kernel is zero. -/
theorem isAwayDegreewise_chartGradedHom (U : X.Opens) :
    Stacks.GradedLocalization.IsAwayDegreewise (chartGradedHom (X := X) n U) 1 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [map_one]
    exact isUnit_one
  · intro k y hy
    refine ⟨0, chartGradedInv n U y, (chartGradedInv n U).map_mem hy, ?_⟩
    rw [pow_zero, one_mul]
    exact congr($(chartGradedHom_comp_inv n U) y)
  · intro k x hx h
    refine ⟨0, ?_⟩
    have hxx : chartGradedInv n U (chartGradedHom n U x) = x :=
      congr($(chartGradedInv_comp_hom n U) x)
    rw [pow_zero, one_mul, ← hxx, h, map_zero]

/-! ### The chartwise module half of Tag 01OE -/

/-- **The inverse image of the integral `𝒪(1)` along the homogeneous coordinates is the
degree-one twist of the chart grading.** This is `Stacks.SymGraded.HasChartTwistOne` at a single
open, with no affineness hypothesis on the open.

The homogeneous coordinates factor through the polynomial ring
`Γ(X, U)[T₀, …, Tₙ]`: first the coefficient change and reindexing
`Stacks.SymGraded.coordGradedHom`, whose twist comparison is an isomorphism by the degree-one
chart argument of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartLocality.isIso_projTwistComparison`, then the graded
isomorphism `Stacks.SymGraded.chartGradedHom`, whose twist comparison is an isomorphism by
`Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.isIso_twistMap`. `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_comp` splits the
inverse image along the composite into the two. -/
theorem nonempty_pullback_chartToProjectiveSpace_iso_twistingSheaf (U : X.Opens) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (chartToProjectiveSpace (X := X) n U)).obj
        (Stacks.AmpleProjectiveImmersion.twistingSheafAtUniverse.{u} n) ≅
      twistingSheaf ((freeSymGradedAlgebra (X := X) (coordIndex.{u} n)).grading U) 1) := by
  have hf := irrelevant_le_map_coordGradedHom (X := X) n U
  have hg := Stacks.GradedRegrading.irrelevant_le_map_of_comp_eq_id
    (chartGradedHom_comp_inv (X := X) n U)
  have h1 : IsIso (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.twistMap (coordGradedHom (X := X) n U) hf 1) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistChartLocality.isIso_projTwistComparison _ _ _ hf 1
      (irrelevant_le_span_image_coordGradedHom n U)
  have h2 : IsIso (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.twistMap (chartGradedHom (X := X) n U) hg 1) :=
    Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.isIso_twistMap _ hg 1 (isAwayDegreewise_chartGradedHom n U)
      SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem
  refine ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map_comp
      (coordGradedHom (X := X) n U) (chartGradedHom (X := X) n U) hf hg)).app _ ≪≫
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map (chartGradedHom (X := X) n U) hg)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map (coordGradedHom (X := X) n U) hf)).app _).symm ≪≫
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map (chartGradedHom (X := X) n U) hg)).mapIso
        (asIso (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.twistMap (coordGradedHom (X := X) n U) hf 1)) ≪≫
    asIso (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.twistMap (chartGradedHom (X := X) n U) hg 1)⟩

/-- **`Stacks.SymGraded.HasChartTwistOne` is a theorem**, at every scheme and every `n`: the
chartwise form of the module half of [Stacks, Tag 01OE] holds. -/
theorem hasChartTwistOne (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : ℕ) : HasChartTwistOne X n :=
  fun U _ => nonempty_pullback_chartToProjectiveSpace_iso_twistingSheaf n U

/-- **The module half of [Stacks, Tag 01OE] over an affine base is a theorem**: the inverse image
of the integral `𝒪(1)` along `Stacks.SymGraded.projectiveBundleToIntegralModel` is the degree-one
twist `𝒪_{𝐏(𝒪_X^{n+1})}(1)` of the projective bundle.

Over an affine base the relative homogeneous spectrum is its own chart over `⊤`, so
`Stacks.SymGraded.hasFreeBundleTwistOne_of_hasChartTwistOne` needs nothing beyond
`Stacks.SymGraded.hasChartTwistOne`. -/
theorem hasFreeBundleTwistOne (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsAffine X] (n : ℕ) :
    HasFreeBundleTwistOne X n :=
  hasFreeBundleTwistOne_of_hasChartTwistOne n (hasChartTwistOne X n)

end Stacks.SymGraded

end
